/*
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Ellele Health vaginal-mucus profile
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

    For Ellele Health vaginal-mucus (VM) batches only. Origin Sciences rectal-mucus
    (RM) batches keep the default database sheet and must NOT use this profile.

        nextflow run originsciences/taxprofiler -profile docker,optimised,ellele ...

    It does two things.

    1. Selects the VM database sheet, which adds a third entry (VMGC) alongside the
       two pluspf entries the RM runs already use.

    2. Names VMGC as reports-only, so its read-level output is not published.

    Why VMGC runs *alongside* pluspf rather than replacing it. VMGC is a
    vagina-restricted reference (786 prokaryotic species-level genome bins), so
    anything that does not belong in a vaginal sample has no correct home in it and
    is either left unclassified or assigned to the nearest vaginal relative.
    Measured on MIC016 (53 VM samples), a median 5.5% of each community -- up to
    29.1% -- falls outside VMGC's coverage, and it is almost entirely reagent and
    environmental contamination. Downstream QC in microbiome-qc therefore reads
    composition and contamination from the comprehensive database, and uses VMGC
    only for Community State Type calling, where its much better vaginal species
    resolution is what matters, and where it is the only reference available to us
    that contains BVAB1.

    Why reports-only. --kraken2_save_reads and --kraken2_save_readclassifications
    are pipeline-wide, so a third database inherits them and would publish its
    classified/unclassified FASTQs and its per-read classifications: roughly 19 GB
    per sample, ~1 TB per batch on MIC016, of which nothing downstream reads a
    single byte. microbiome-qc consumes per-read output from db1 only, and needs
    just the Bracken report from VMGC. The files are still written to the work
    directory, which is cleaned; they are simply not copied to the results bucket.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/

params {
    databases                = 's3://orisci-data-public/taxprofiler-v1.2.3/taxprofiler_db_kraken2_VM.csv'
    kraken2_reports_only_dbs = 'vmgc'
}
